  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 202 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nWednesday into the weekend, we can expect hot temperatures in the \nupper 90s to lower 100s to continue as the overall Four Corners high \nwill remain in place. That being said, as the flow becomes more \nnorthwesterly our chances of precipitation pick up to about medium \n(40-50%) on Wednesday and those chances hold steady on Thursday, \nwith a little bit of a drop off on Friday.  Then as we head into the \nweekend, we look to dry back out as the high expands further east \nmore over the Rockies to southern high plains.  This will lead to \nhot temperatures and a more dry northerly to northeasterly flow over \nthe Panhandles.  \n\nWeber",
